    "created_at": "2015-09-25T16:29:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-25T16:29:48Z",
    "body": "Making WebSocket run over Fetch is a non-starter unless we fork the whole protocol back in. (It does seem that this might be needed at some point, e.g., presumably `rel=preconnect` also works for WebSocket.)\n\nSo I guess maybe for now we should continue to duplicate requirements.\n\nIt seems @mikewest has already done so in https://w3c.github.io/webappsec/specs/upgrade/#websockets-integration. So maybe we should turn that into a monkey patch for HTML instead.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/143269731/reactions",
